// Config.xcconfig — committed base configuration for the SceneViewDemo app
// target (Debug + Release). Its only job is to *optionally* pull in the
// developer-local, gitignored `Secrets.xcconfig` so a keyed build is possible
// from Xcode (and `xcodebuild`) without editing the scheme or this file.
//
// HOW THE SKETCHFAB KEY REACHES THE APP (#2356, mirrors Android #2343)
// --------------------------------------------------------------------
// `Info.plist` declares  SketchfabAPIKey = $(SKETCHFAB_API_KEY)  so the build
// substitutes whatever the `SKETCHFAB_API_KEY` *build setting* resolves to.
// There are three ways that setting gets a value, in increasing precedence:
//
//   1. (this file) `#include?` of `Secrets.xcconfig` — the local-dev path.
//      Copy `Secrets.xcconfig.template` → `Secrets.xcconfig` (gitignored),
//      paste your token, and every Xcode/`xcodebuild` build is keyed.
//   2. The legacy scheme env var `SKETCHFAB_API_KEY` (Edit Scheme → Run →
//      Arguments → Environment Variables) — read by `SketchfabConfig` via
//      `ProcessInfo` at runtime. Works under Xcode "Run" only, not archives.
//   3. A command-line build setting: `xcodebuild ... SKETCHFAB_API_KEY=…`.
//      This OVERRIDES the xcconfig, so CI (`app-store.yml`, `ios.yml`) and the
//      device-QA harness (`ios-device-qa.sh --sketchfab-key`) inject the secret
//      this way without ever writing a file to disk.
//
// SECURITY: the real token lives ONLY in the gitignored `Secrets.xcconfig`
// (or the env / a CLI arg). This file and `Secrets.xcconfig.template` carry
// NO secret and are safe to commit. `.gitignore` already excludes
// `**/Secrets.xcconfig`.
//
// The `?` makes the include OPTIONAL: a fresh checkout WITHOUT `Secrets.xcconfig`
// builds keyless and silently (no "unable to open base configuration" warning),
// exactly as before — the Explore/Sketchfab path is simply disabled until a key
// is supplied. See `SketchfabConfig.swift` and the "Keyed QA" section of
// `.maestro/README.md`.
// FIREBASE CONFIG (analytics, Crashlytics, push — demo app only)
// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// `GoogleService-Info.plist` is NEVER committed (public repo; `.gitignore` has
// `**/GoogleService-Info.plist`). The "Embed Firebase config" build phase copies it
// into the app bundle from, in this order:
//
//   1. `SV_GOOGLE_SERVICE_INFO_PLIST` — an absolute path, as a build setting
//      (`xcodebuild ... SV_GOOGLE_SERVICE_INFO_PLIST=/path/GoogleService-Info.plist`;
//      `app-store.yml` decodes the `DEMO_GOOGLE_SERVICE_INFO_PLIST_BASE64` secret
//      there) or set in the gitignored `Secrets.xcconfig`;
//   2. `SceneViewDemo/GoogleService-Info.plist` next to this file (gitignored).
//
// With neither, the app is built without Firebase: `FirebaseTelemetry.start()` finds
// no plist, never calls `FirebaseApp.configure()`, analytics stays a no-op and the
// push pre-prompt and the Privacy switches are hidden. Such a build cannot crash on
// Firebase. An App Store archive (`ACTION=install`, Release) fails instead — a store
// build without analytics is usually a mistake — unless `SV_ALLOW_MISSING_FIREBASE=1`
// (what `app-store.yml` passes, with a warning, when the secret is empty) or
// `SV_ALLOW_MISSING_SECRETS=1` (forks, local Release builds).
SV_GOOGLE_SERVICE_INFO_PLIST =

#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
